# Build artifacts.
# Anchored with a leading slash: an unanchored `xlogin` also matches pam.d/xlogin, which is a
# tracked, required config file.
/xlogin
/tools/uirender
*.o
*.d
# ...which also matches the pam.d DIRECTORY, so a new PAM file there would be silently left
# out of every commit. pam.d/xlogin only escaped it by being tracked before this rule existed.
!/pam.d/
*.so
*.a
build/
dist/

# Release tarballs
simple-login-gui-*.tar.gz
simple-login-gui-*/

# Local-only development documents and tooling. None of these reach a clone or a release
# tarball, so no tracked file may name one -- the phase gate checks that over `git ls-files`.
CLAUDE.md
RULES.md
PLAN.md
SECURITY.md
task.md
.claude/

# Editor backups
*~
*.swp
*.swo
*.tar.gz
